sentences.l:
I-longed-for him-whom I-love, and-when I-saw-him * I-was-stunned and-not I-had-mastery-of a-tongue nor an-eye;
And-I-lowered in-reverence for-him and-awe, * and-I-tried to I-hide that-which in-me, and-not it-was-hidden;
And-indeed there-was with-me for-reproach registers, * and-when we-met, not I-uttered nor a-letter.

To-you in the-hearts a-secret not it-appears, * folded-away, hidden, not it-is-unrolled;
O shamer-of the-moon the-shining with-his-beauty, * and-by-his-loveliness is-likened the-morning the-radiant;
In light-of your-face (are) desires not they-end, * and-haunts ever they-increase and-multiply;
I-melt from burning while-your-face (is) my-paradise, * and-I-die from thirst while-your-saliva (is) Kawthar.
